 >>[2026-03-20 14:59] observe — the new dist lane produces runnable JS and a versioned manifest, but it still has no declarations or type-aware export metadata.
 >>[2026-03-20 15:00] observe — TypeScript can emit a coherent declaration tree for the public runtime/parser entrypoints when driven through a tsconfig-based compile, including the internal relative imports those entrypoints depend on.
 >>[2026-03-20 15:00] decide — the first publish-hardening step should emit dist/types plus small top-level declaration facades rather than trying to flatten or bundle all declarations.
 >>[2026-03-20 15:00] taste — declarations should expose the public contract cleanly while preserving the existing package seams, not invent a second type topology.
}

